  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is dropped from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> on a light horizontal platform fixed to one end of an elastic spring, the other being fixed to a base, as shown in the diagram. The particle collides with the platform and sticks to it. As a result, the spring is compressed by an amount <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. What is the force constant of the spring?<br />\r(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0055_7a23b7e56a7a.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 157px;\" />"
  },
